body:
#### PR description:

This PR introduces `AoSWrapper` as a nested class of the SoA layout. It provides the same utilities as the SoA class, i.e., `View`, `ConstView`, and `Metadata`, making it a suitable template for `PortableCollections`. The `View` of the `AoSWrapper` class comes with a `transpose` function that copies an element at index i from an `SoA::ConstView` to the `AoSWrapper`.  This function is used to add a `transpose` function to the `PortableCollections` which copies all data from an SoA layout to an AoS layout. The functionality is also added to transpose from an AoS layout to an SoA layout. 

The idea of this PR was previously introduced by @leobeltra in [#49072](https://github.com/cms-sw/cmssw/pull/49072). This PR sharpens the implementation by closing misalignments between the SoA View and AoS View and strongly extending the test cases to ensure that both work in the same way. Furthermore, SoA element and View methods are now aligned between the SoA and AoS versions as well, and the AoS ConstView can be used together with the `SoAMultiView` introduced [here](https://github.com/cms-sw/cmssw/pull/51458).

The data members of the `AoSWrapper` are also designed in a way that they can easily be serialized by ROOT. This means Eigen objects are not directly part of the `aos_` data member. Instead, Eigen objects are represented by `std::array<ScalarType, Row * Cols>` on the buffer, and `Eigen::Map` is used for the data access in the View. ROOT I/O and schema evolution are tested by a set of tests used for the SoA version as well


Furthermore, the layout of the `TrackingRecHitsSoACollection` is switched from an SoA to an AoS layout. This means that the input to the CA extension uses an AoS data layout with the changes proposed by this PR. The changes have been benchmarked using the following workflow:

```
cmsDriver.py Phase2 -s L1P2GT,HLT:75e33_trackingOnly \
         --processName=HLTX \
         --conditions auto:phase2_realistic_T35 \
         --geometry ExtendedRun4D110 \
         --era Phase2C17I13M9 \
         --customise SLHCUpgradeSimulations/Configuration/aging.customise_aging_1000 \
         --eventcontent FEVTDEBUGHLT \
         --filein=$ALL_FILES \
         --mc \
         --inputCommands="keep *, drop *_hlt*_*_HLT, drop triggerTriggerFilterObjectWithRefs_l1t*_*_HLT" \
         -n 1000 \
         --procModifiers ngtScouting \
         --no_exec \
         --output={} \
         --python_filename timing_config.py
```

The benchmark was executed as `patatrack-scripts/benchmark --preset hltPhase2 --nvidia-mps -- timing_config.py` on a full node of the NGT cluster using 4 x NVIDIA L40S GPUS and 2 x AMD EPYC 9534 64-Core Processors with 16 jobs, 16 threads, and 16 streams and using NVIDIA MPS active thread percentage: 16 job(s) @ 25%. 

This PR suggests using an AoS layout for the `TrackingRecHitsSoACollection`, which increases the throughput to `442.1 ev/s` from the default `345.5 ev/s`. This means the workflow can profit from a higher throughput using the AoS layout and running on GPU. Equivalent measurements on CPU only showed no significant difference between the AoS and the SoA data layout in this case. 

Using nsight compute to profile the kernels shows that most of the improvements reported here come from fewer cache misses in the AoS version. Exemplarily, the memory chart of the [GetDoubletsFromHisto kernel is shown here](https://github.com/cms-sw/cmssw/blob/cecbb6f0b14f31365b23ecf5ec702f4990cad268/RecoTracker/PixelSeeding/plugins/alpaka/CAPixelDoubletsAlgos.h#L169). The reason why the AoS layout achieves better cache utilization here might be too random memory accesses. 

<img width="2125" height="971" alt="Screenshot 2026-10-14 at 14 56 34" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c94247d2-d44d-4f47-b415-1f1bc27db1e4" />

The total GPU memory consumption of the benchmarks is shown here:
<img width="4800" height="2700" alt="GPUMemoryUsageSoAvsAoS" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6f2df98f-7e34-4f76-ab19-a9f5bcd6ae76" />

It shows slightly higher peaks (about 1GB) for the AoS version.

In the following, a full SoA class is appended after running the preprocessor step. The SoA that is shown is defined as:

```c++
GENERATE_SOA_LAYOUT(SoALayout1, 
    SOA_COLUMN(int, column), 
    SOA_EIGEN_COLUMN(Eigen::Vector3d, vector), 
    SOA_SCALAR(int, id))
```


<details>
<summary>Click for a full definition of SoALayout1</summary>

```c++
template <std::size_t ALIGNMENT = cms::soa::CacheLineSize::defaultSize,
          bool ALIGNMENT_ENFORCEMENT = cms::soa::AlignmentEnforcement::relaxed>
struct SoALayout1 {
  using self_type = SoALayout1;
  using AlignmentEnforcement = cms::soa::AlignmentEnforcement;
  using size_type = cms::soa::size_type;
  using byte_size_type = cms::soa::byte_size_type;
  constexpr static byte_size_type defaultAlignment = 128;
  constexpr static byte_size_type alignment = ALIGNMENT;
  constexpr static bool alignmentEnforcement = ALIGNMENT_ENFORCEMENT;
  constexpr static byte_size_type conditionalAlignment =
      alignmentEnforcement == cms::soa::AlignmentEnforcement::enforced ? alignment : 0;
  constexpr static bool isSoA = true;
  template <cms::soa::SoAColumnType COLUMN_TYPE, class C>
  using SoAValueWithConf = cms::soa::SoAValue<COLUMN_TYPE, C, conditionalAlignment>;
  template <cms::soa::SoAColumnType COLUMN_TYPE, class C>
  using SoAConstValueWithConf = cms::soa::SoAConstValue<COLUMN_TYPE, C, conditionalAlignment>;
  template <std::size_t VIEW_ALIGNMENT = cms::soa::CacheLineSize::defaultSize,
            bool VIEW_ALIGNMENT_ENFORCEMENT = cms::soa::AlignmentEnforcement::relaxed,
            bool RESTRICT_QUALIFY = cms::soa::RestrictQualify::Default,
            cms::soa::RangeChecking::Mode RANGE_CHECKING = cms::soa::RangeChecking::Default>
  struct ViewTemplateFreeParams;
  void soaToStreamInternal(std::ostream& _soa_impl_os) const {
    _soa_impl_os << "SoALayout1"
                    "("
                 << elements_ << " elements, byte alignement= " << alignment << ", @" << mem_ << "): " << std::endl;
    _soa_impl_os << "  sizeof("
                    "SoALayout1"
                    "): "
                 << sizeof(SoALayout1) << std::endl;
    byte_size_type _soa_impl_offset = 0;
    cms::soa::detail::PrintColumn<typename Metadata::ParametersTypeOf_column>{}(
        _soa_impl_os, "column", _soa_impl_offset, elements_, alignment);
    cms::soa::detail::PrintColumn<typename Metadata::ParametersTypeOf_vector>{}(
        _soa_impl_os, "vector", _soa_impl_offset, elements_, alignment);
    cms::soa::detail::PrintColumn<typename Metadata::ParametersTypeOf_id>{}(
        _soa_impl_os, "id", _soa_impl_offset, elements_, alignment);
    _soa_impl_os << "Final offset = " << _soa_impl_offset << " computeDataSize(...): " << computeDataSize(elements_)
                 << std::endl;
    _soa_impl_os << std::endl;
  }
  static constexpr byte_size_type computeDataSize(size_type elements) {
    byte_size_type _soa_impl_ret = 0;
    _soa_impl_ret += cms::soa::detail::ComputePitch<typename Metadata::ParametersTypeOf_column>{}(elements, alignment);
    _soa_impl_ret += cms::soa::detail::ComputePitch<typename Metadata::ParametersTypeOf_vector>{}(elements, alignment);
    _soa_impl_ret += cms::soa::detail::ComputePitch<typename Metadata::ParametersTypeOf_id>{}(elements, alignment);
    return _soa_impl_ret;
  }
  struct RecordType {
    int column_;
    cms::soa::detail::EigenRecordType<Eigen::Vector3d> vector_;
  };
  struct Metadata {
    friend SoALayout1;
    inline __attribute__((always_inline)) size_type size() const { return parent_.elements_; }
    inline __attribute__((always_inline)) byte_size_type byteSize() const { return parent_.byteSize_; }
    inline __attribute__((always_inline)) byte_size_type alignment() const { return SoALayout1::alignment; }
    inline __attribute__((always_inline)) std::byte* data() { return parent_.mem_; }
    inline __attribute__((always_inline)) const std::byte* data() const { return parent_.mem_; }
    inline __attribute__((always_inline)) std::byte* nextByte() const { return parent_.mem_ + parent_.byteSize_; }
    inline __attribute__((always_inline)) SoALayout1 cloneToNewAddress(std::byte* _soa_impl_addr) const {
      return SoALayout1(_soa_impl_addr, parent_.elements_);
    }
    constexpr static cms::soa::SoAColumnType ColumnTypeOf_column = cms::soa::SoAColumnType::column;
    using ParametersTypeOf_column = cms::soa::SoAParameters_ColumnType<cms::soa::SoAColumnType::column>::DataType<int>;
    inline __attribute__((always_inline)) ParametersTypeOf_column parametersOf_column() const {
      return ParametersTypeOf_column(reinterpret_cast<cms::soa::detail::EnumTraits<int>::type*>(parent_.column_));
    }
    inline __attribute__((always_inline)) auto* addressOf_column() {
      return parent_.metadata().parametersOf_column().addr_;
    }
    inline __attribute__((always_inline)) const auto* addressOf_column() const {
      return parent_.metadata().parametersOf_column().addr_;
    }
    inline __attribute__((always_inline)) byte_size_type columnPitch() const {
      return cms::soa::detail::ComputePitch<ParametersTypeOf_column>{}(parent_.elements_, ParentClass::alignment);
    }
    constexpr static cms::soa::SoAColumnType ColumnTypeOf_vector = cms::soa::SoAColumnType::eigen;
    using ParametersTypeOf_vector =
        cms::soa::SoAParameters_ColumnType<cms::soa::SoAColumnType::eigen>::DataType<Eigen::Vector3d>;
    inline __attribute__((always_inline)) ParametersTypeOf_vector parametersOf_vector() const {
      return ParametersTypeOf_vector(parent_.vector_, parent_.vectorStride_);
    }
    inline __attribute__((always_inline)) auto* addressOf_vector() {
      return parent_.metadata().parametersOf_vector().addr_;
    }
    inline __attribute__((always_inline)) const auto* addressOf_vector() const {
      return parent_.metadata().parametersOf_vector().addr_;
    }
    inline __attribute__((always_inline)) byte_size_type vectorPitch() const {
      return cms::soa::detail::ComputePitch<ParametersTypeOf_vector>{}(parent_.elements_, ParentClass::alignment);
    }
    constexpr static cms::soa::SoAColumnType ColumnTypeOf_id = cms::soa::SoAColumnType::scalar;
    using ParametersTypeOf_id = cms::soa::SoAParameters_ColumnType<cms::soa::SoAColumnType::scalar>::DataType<int>;
    inline __attribute__((always_inline)) ParametersTypeOf_id parametersOf_id() const {
      return ParametersTypeOf_id(reinterpret_cast<cms::soa::detail::EnumTraits<int>::type*>(parent_.id_));
    }
    inline __attribute__((always_inline)) auto* addressOf_id() { return parent_.metadata().parametersOf_id().addr_; }
    inline __attribute__((always_inline)) const auto* addressOf_id() const {
      return parent_.metadata().parametersOf_id().addr_;
    }
    inline __attribute__((always_inline)) byte_size_type idPitch() const {
      return cms::soa::detail::ComputePitch<ParametersTypeOf_id>{}(parent_.elements_, ParentClass::alignment);
    }
    struct value_element {
      inline __attribute__((always_inline)) value_element(int column, Eigen::Vector3d vector)
          : column_{column}, vector_{vector} {}
      inline __attribute__((always_inline)) value_element(const SoALayout1::RecordType& record)
          : column_{record.column_}, vector_{cms::soa::EigenConstMap<Eigen::Vector3d>((record.vector_).data())} {}
      int column_;
      Eigen::Vector3d vector_;
    };
    Metadata& operator=(const Metadata&) = delete;
    Metadata(const Metadata&) = delete;

  private:
    inline __attribute__((always_inline)) Metadata(const SoALayout1& _soa_impl_parent) : parent_(_soa_impl_parent) {}
    const SoALayout1& parent_;
    using ParentClass = SoALayout1;
  };
  inline __attribute__((always_inline)) const Metadata metadata() const { return Metadata(*this); }
  inline __attribute__((always_inline)) Metadata metadata() { return Metadata(*this); }
  template <std::size_t VIEW_ALIGNMENT,
            bool VIEW_ALIGNMENT_ENFORCEMENT,
            bool RESTRICT_QUALIFY,
            cms::soa::RangeChecking::Mode RANGE_CHECKING>
  struct ConstViewTemplateFreeParams {
    using SoALayout1_parametrized = SoALayout1<VIEW_ALIGNMENT, VIEW_ALIGNMENT_ENFORCEMENT>;
    using size_type = cms::soa::size_type;
    using byte_size_type = cms::soa::byte_size_type;
    using AlignmentEnforcement = cms::soa::AlignmentEnforcement;
    template <std::size_t, bool, bool, cms::soa::RangeChecking::Mode>
    friend struct ViewTemplateFreeParams;
    constexpr static byte_size_type defaultAlignment = cms::soa::CacheLineSize::defaultSize;
    constexpr static byte_size_type alignment = VIEW_ALIGNMENT;
    constexpr static bool alignmentEnforcement = VIEW_ALIGNMENT_ENFORCEMENT;
    constexpr static byte_size_type conditionalAlignment =
        alignmentEnforcement == AlignmentEnforcement::enforced ? alignment : 0;
    constexpr static bool restrictQualify = RESTRICT_QUALIFY;
    constexpr static cms::soa::RangeChecking::Mode rangeChecking = RANGE_CHECKING;
    constexpr static bool isSoA = SoALayout1_parametrized::isSoA;
    struct Metadata {
      friend ConstViewTemplateFreeParams;
      inline __attribute__((always_inline)) size_type size() const { return parent_.elements_; }
      using TypeOf_Layout = SoALayout1_parametrized;
      using ParametersTypeOf_column = typename TypeOf_Layout::Metadata::ParametersTypeOf_column;
      using TypeOf_column = int;
      constexpr static cms::soa::SoAColumnType ColumnTypeOf_column = TypeOf_Layout::Metadata::ColumnTypeOf_column;
      inline __attribute__((always_inline)) const auto parametersOf_column() const {
        return (parent_.columnParameters_);
      };
      using ParametersTypeOf_vector = typename TypeOf_Layout::Metadata::ParametersTypeOf_vector;
      using TypeOf_vector = Eigen::Vector3d;
      constexpr static cms::soa::SoAColumnType ColumnTypeOf_vector = TypeOf_Layout::Metadata::ColumnTypeOf_vector;
      inline __attribute__((always_inline)) const auto parametersOf_vector() const {
        return (parent_.vectorParameters_);
      };
      using ParametersTypeOf_id = typename TypeOf_Layout::Metadata::ParametersTypeOf_id;
      using TypeOf_id = int;
      constexpr static cms::soa::SoAColumnType ColumnTypeOf_id = TypeOf_Layout::Metadata::ColumnTypeOf_id;
      inline __attribute__((always_inline)) const auto parametersOf_id() const { return (parent_.idParameters_); };
      inline __attribute__((always_inline)) auto const* addressOf_column() const {
        return parent_.columnParameters_.addr_;
      };
      inline __attribute__((always_inline)) auto const* addressOf_vector() const {
        return parent_.vectorParameters_.addr_;
      };
      inline __attribute__((always_inline)) auto const* addressOf_id() const { return parent_.idParameters_.addr_; };
      Metadata& operator=(const Metadata&) = delete;
      Metadata(const Metadata&) = delete;

    private:
      inline __attribute__((always_inline)) Metadata(const ConstViewTemplateFreeParams& _soa_impl_parent)
          : parent_(_soa_impl_parent) {}
      const ConstViewTemplateFreeParams& parent_;
    };
    struct Metarecords {
      friend ConstViewTemplateFreeParams;
      inline __attribute__((always_inline)) Metarecords(const ConstViewTemplateFreeParams& _soa_impl_parent)
          : parent_(_soa_impl_parent),
            column_{parent_.metadata().parametersOf_column()},
            vector_{parent_.metadata().parametersOf_vector()},
            id_{parent_.metadata().parametersOf_id()} {}
      cms::soa::ConstTuple<typename Metadata::ParametersTypeOf_column>::Type column() const {
        return std::make_tuple(column_, parent_.elements_);
      }
      cms::soa::ConstTuple<typename Metadata::ParametersTypeOf_vector>::Type vector() const {
        return std::make_tuple(vector_, parent_.elements_);
      }
      cms::soa::ConstTuple<typename Metadata::ParametersTypeOf_id>::Type id() const {
        return std::make_tuple(id_, parent_.elements_);
      }

    private:
      const ConstViewTemplateFreeParams& parent_;
      typename Metadata::ParametersTypeOf_column::ConstType column_;
      typename Metadata::ParametersTypeOf_vector::ConstType vector_;
      typename Metadata::ParametersTypeOf_id::ConstType id_;
    };
    inline __attribute__((always_inline)) const Metadata metadata() const { return Metadata(*this); }
    inline __attribute__((always_inline)) const Metarecords records() const { return Metarecords(*this); }
    ConstViewTemplateFreeParams() = default;
    ConstViewTemplateFreeParams(const Metadata::TypeOf_Layout& layout)
        : elements_(layout.elements_),
          columnParameters_([&]() -> auto {
            auto params = layout.metadata().parametersOf_column();
            if constexpr (alignmentEnforcement == AlignmentEnforcement::enforced)
              cms::soa::detail::checkAlignment(params.data(),
                                               alignment,
                                               "In constructor by layout: misaligned column: "
                                               "column");
            return params;
          }()),
          vectorParameters_([&]() -> auto {
            auto params = layout.metadata().parametersOf_vector();
            if constexpr (alignmentEnforcement == AlignmentEnforcement::enforced)
              cms::soa::detail::checkAlignment(params.data(),
                                               alignment,
                                               "In constructor by layout: misaligned column: "
                                               "vector");
            return params;
          }()),
          idParameters_([&]() -> auto {
            auto params = layout.metadata().parametersOf_id();
            if constexpr (alignmentEnforcement == AlignmentEnforcement::enforced)
              cms::soa::detail::checkAlignment(params.data(),
                                               alignment,
                                               "In constructor by layout: misaligned column: "
                                               "id");
            return params;
          }()) {}
    ConstViewTemplateFreeParams(cms::soa::ConstTuple<typename Metadata::ParametersTypeOf_column>::Type column,
                                cms::soa::ConstTuple<typename Metadata::ParametersTypeOf_vector>::Type vector,
                                cms::soa::ConstTuple<typename Metadata::ParametersTypeOf_id>::Type id) {
      bool readyToSet = false;
      if (not readyToSet) {
        elements_ = std::get<1>(column);
        readyToSet = true;
      }
      columnParameters_ = [&]() -> auto {
        if (elements_ != std::get<1>(column))
          cms::soa::detail::throwRuntimeError(
              "In constructor by column pointers: number of elements not equal for every column: "
              "column");
        if constexpr (alignmentEnforcement == AlignmentEnforcement::enforced)
          cms::soa::detail::checkAlignment(std::get<0>(column).data(),
                                           alignment,
                                           "In constructor by column: misaligned column: "
                                           "column");
        return std::get<0>(column);
      }();
      if (not readyToSet) {
        elements_ = std::get<1>(vector);
        readyToSet = true;
      }
      vectorParameters_ = [&]() -> auto {
        if (cms::soa::alignSize(elements_ * sizeof(Eigen::Vector3d::Scalar), alignment) /
                sizeof(Eigen::Vector3d::Scalar) !=
            std::get<0>(vector).stride_) {
          cms::soa::detail::throwRuntimeError(
              "In constructor by column pointers: stride not equal between eigen columns: "
              "vector");
        }
        if (elements_ != std::get<1>(vector))
          cms::soa::detail::throwRuntimeError(
              "In constructor by column pointers: number of elements not equal for every column: "
              "vector");
        if constexpr (alignmentEnforcement == AlignmentEnforcement::enforced)
          cms::soa::detail::checkAlignment(std::get<0>(vector).data(),
                                           alignment,
                                           "In constructor by column: misaligned column: "
                                           "vector");
        return std::get<0>(vector);
      }();
      if (not readyToSet) {
        elements_ = std::get<1>(id);
        readyToSet = true;
      }
      idParameters_ = [&]() -> auto {
        if (elements_ != std::get<1>(id))
          cms::soa::detail::throwRuntimeError(
              "In constructor by column pointers: number of elements not equal for every column: "
              "id");
        if constexpr (alignmentEnforcement == AlignmentEnforcement::enforced)
          cms::soa::detail::checkAlignment(std::get<0>(id).data(),
                                           alignment,
                                           "In constructor by column: misaligned column: "
                                           "id");
        return std::get<0>(id);
      }();
    }
    ConstViewTemplateFreeParams(ConstViewTemplateFreeParams const&) = default;
    ConstViewTemplateFreeParams& operator=(ConstViewTemplateFreeParams const&) = default;
    template <std::size_t OTHER_VIEW_ALIGNMENT,
              bool OTHER_VIEW_ALIGNMENT_ENFORCEMENT,
              bool OTHER_RESTRICT_QUALIFY,
              cms::soa::RangeChecking::Mode OTHER_RANGE_CHECKING>
    ConstViewTemplateFreeParams(ConstViewTemplateFreeParams<OTHER_VIEW_ALIGNMENT,
                                                            OTHER_VIEW_ALIGNMENT_ENFORCEMENT,
                                                            OTHER_RESTRICT_QUALIFY,
                                                            OTHER_RANGE_CHECKING> const& other)
        : ConstViewTemplateFreeParams{other.elements_,
                                      cms::soa::const_cast_SoAParametersImpl(other.columnParameters_),
                                      cms::soa::const_cast_SoAParametersImpl(other.vectorParameters_),
                                      cms::soa::const_cast_SoAParametersImpl(other.idParameters_)} {}
    ConstViewTemplateFreeParams(size_type elems,
                                Metadata::ParametersTypeOf_column::ConstType column,
                                Metadata::ParametersTypeOf_vector::ConstType vector,
                                Metadata::ParametersTypeOf_id::ConstType id)
        : elements_{elems}, columnParameters_{column}, vectorParameters_{vector}, idParameters_{id} {}
    template <std::size_t OTHER_VIEW_ALIGNMENT,
              bool OTHER_VIEW_ALIGNMENT_ENFORCEMENT,
              bool OTHER_RESTRICT_QUALIFY,
              cms::soa::RangeChecking::Mode OTHER_RANGE_CHECKING>
    ConstViewTemplateFreeParams& operator=(ConstViewTemplateFreeParams<OTHER_VIEW_ALIGNMENT,
                                                                       OTHER_VIEW_ALIGNMENT_ENFORCEMENT,
                                                                       OTHER_RESTRICT_QUALIFY,
                                                                       OTHER_RANGE_CHECKING> const& other) {
      *this = other;
    }
    ConstViewTemplateFreeParams(ConstViewTemplateFreeParams&&) = default;
    ConstViewTemplateFreeParams& operator=(ConstViewTemplateFreeParams&&) = default;
    ~ConstViewTemplateFreeParams() = default;
    struct const_element {
      inline __attribute__((always_inline)) const_element(
          size_type _soa_impl_index,
          const typename Metadata::ParametersTypeOf_column::ConstType column,
          const typename Metadata::ParametersTypeOf_vector::ConstType vector)
          : column_(_soa_impl_index, column), vector_(_soa_impl_index, vector) {}
      inline __attribute__((always_inline)) const typename cms::soa::SoAConstValue_ColumnType<
          Metadata::ColumnTypeOf_column>::template DataType<typename Metadata::TypeOf_column>::
          template Alignment<conditionalAlignment>::template ConstValue<restrictQualify>::RefToConst
          column() const {
        return column_();
      }
      inline __attribute__((always_inline)) const typename cms::soa::SoAConstValue_ColumnType<
          Metadata::ColumnTypeOf_vector>::template DataType<typename Metadata::TypeOf_vector>::
          template Alignment<conditionalAlignment>::template ConstValue<restrictQualify>::RefToConst
          vector() const {
        return vector_();
      }

    private:
      const cms::soa::ConstValueTraitsFromC<typename cms::soa::SoAConstValue_ColumnType<Metadata::ColumnTypeOf_column>::
                                                template DataType<typename Metadata::TypeOf_column>::template Alignment<
                                                    conditionalAlignment>::template ConstValue<restrictQualify>>
          column_;
      const cms::soa::ConstValueTraitsFromC<typename cms::soa::SoAConstValue_ColumnType<Metadata::ColumnTypeOf_vector>::
                                                template DataType<typename Metadata::TypeOf_vector>::template Alignment<
                                                    conditionalAlignment>::template ConstValue<restrictQualify>>
          vector_;
    };
    inline __attribute__((always_inline)) const const_element
    operator[](cms::soa::detail::IndexWithSourceLocation<rangeChecking> _soa_impl_index) const {
      if constexpr (rangeChecking != cms::soa::RangeChecking::disabled) {
        if (_soa_impl_index.value_ >= elements_ or _soa_impl_index.value_ < 0) {
          cms::soa::detail::throwOutOfRangeError<decltype(_soa_impl_index)::mode>(
              ("Out of range index in ConstViewTemplateFreeParams "
               "SoALayout1"
               "::operator[]"),
              (_soa_impl_index),
              (elements_));
        }
      }
      return const_element{_soa_impl_index.value_, columnParameters_, vectorParameters_};
    }
    inline __attribute__((always_inline))
    typename cms::soa::SoAAccessors<typename Metadata::TypeOf_column>::template ColumnType<
        Metadata::ColumnTypeOf_column>::template AccessType<cms::soa::SoAAccessType::constAccess>::
        template Alignment<conditionalAlignment>::template RestrictQualifier<restrictQualify>::NoParamReturnType
        column() const {
      return typename cms::soa::SoAAccessors<typename Metadata::TypeOf_column>::template ColumnType<
          Metadata::ColumnTypeOf_column>::template AccessType<cms::soa::SoAAccessType::constAccess>::
          template Alignment<conditionalAlignment>::template RestrictQualifier<restrictQualify>(columnParameters_,
                                                                                                elements_)();
    }
    inline __attribute__((always_inline))
    typename cms::soa::SoAAccessors<typename Metadata::TypeOf_column>::template ColumnType<
        Metadata::ColumnTypeOf_column>::template AccessType<cms::soa::SoAAccessType::constAccess>::
        template Alignment<conditionalAlignment>::template RestrictQualifier<restrictQualify>::ParamReturnType
        column(cms::soa::detail::IndexWithSourceLocation<rangeChecking> _soa_impl_index) const {
      if constexpr (rangeChecking != cms::soa::RangeChecking::disabled) {
        if (_soa_impl_index.value_ >= elements_ or _soa_impl_index.value_ < 0) {
          cms::soa::detail::throwOutOfRangeError<decltype(_soa_impl_index)::mode>(("Out of range index in mutable "
                                                                                   "column"
                                                                                   "(size_type index)"),
                                                                                  (_soa_impl_index),
                                                                                  (elements_));
        }
      }
      return typename cms::soa::SoAAccessors<typename Metadata::TypeOf_column>::template ColumnType<
          Metadata::ColumnTypeOf_column>::template AccessType<cms::soa::SoAAccessType::constAccess>::
          template Alignment<conditionalAlignment>::template RestrictQualifier<restrictQualify>(
              columnParameters_, elements_)(_soa_impl_index.value_);
    }
    inline __attribute__((always_inline))
    typename cms::soa::SoAAccessors<typename Metadata::TypeOf_vector>::template ColumnType<
        Metadata::ColumnTypeOf_vector>::template AccessType<cms::soa::SoAAccessType::constAccess>::
        template Alignment<conditionalAlignment>::template RestrictQualifier<restrictQualify>::NoParamReturnType
        vector() const {
